 "notes": "Source: TARS-Net Telangana State AMR Surveillance Annual Report 2024 (nodal centre Osmania Medical College), 13 sentinel sites, 10 districts, 16,274 isolates (15,674 unique-patient after dedup), Jan 1–Dec 31 2024. Tables report %RESISTANT (%R) per specimen column; ALL s-values here were converted s=100−R (from_R:true). Guidelines: CLSI. Specimen scope for each organism entry is the table's per-specimen N (BLOOD or URINE). I extracted blood (sterile-site benchmark) for all six core organisms, plus urine for E. coli, Klebsiella and Enterococcus (UTI-relevant). Tables 6–11 = S.aureus/Enterococcus/E.coli/Klebsiella/Pseudomonas/Acinetobacter. Report labels genus-level \"Klebsiella species\", \"Pseudomonas species\", \"Acinetobacter species\", \"Enterococcus species\" (species not split) — mapped to K. pneumoniae / P. aeruginosa / A. baumannii as the dominant species and to generic \"Enterococcus\". MRSA context: cefoxitin %R (methicillin surrogate) = 53% in blood, 43% in pus, 100% in OSBF(n=4) for S. aureus; so MRSA ~53% among blood isolates. VRE: Enterococcus vancomycin %R = 3% blood, 0.26% urine, 2% pus. Linezolid 0%R across all specimens for both S.aureus and Enterococcus. Colistin 0%R (100%S)",
